Blender on Haiku: find the data files next to the executable when started through a link

Tracker and the Deskbar start a program through a link (the Deskbar's Applications entries are links)
with the link's path as argv[0]. On Haiku where_am_i() takes argv[0] as the program path, so Blender
looked for 3.6/ next to the link: no scripts, no fonts, "No module named 'bpy'" and an abort a second
after start. Resolve the link (realpath) as binreloc does on Linux.

--- a/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/appdir.c
+++ b/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/appdir.c
@@ -880,6 +880,17 @@
     }
     /* Remove "/./" and "/../" so string comparisons can be used on the path. */
     BLI_path_normalize_native(program_filepath);
+#  ifdef __HAIKU__
+    /* Tracker and the Deskbar start a program through a link (the Deskbar's menu entries are
+     * links) with the link's path as `argv[0]`: the data files are next to the executable. */
+    {
+      char *resolved = realpath(program_filepath, NULL);
+      if (resolved) {
+        BLI_strncpy(program_filepath, resolved, program_filepath_maxncpy);
+        free(resolved);
+      }
+    }
+#  endif
 
 #  if defined(DEBUG)
     if (!STREQ(program_name, program_filepath)) {
